Error [jet.MoveWithoutMarker]: `eat` takes `v`, but `v` is used again later
  --> Tests/UI/Hardening/user_struct_named_noclone_is_still_cloneable.jet:9:9
    |
  9 |     eat(v)
    |         ^
  --> Tests/UI/Hardening/user_struct_named_noclone_is_still_cloneable.jet:10:13
    |
 10 |     print(v.n)
    |             ^ `v` is used again here
 Why: `eat` takes ownership of this argument, and a call never copies on its own, so `v` has no value after this call
 Fix: Write `v.copy()` to pass a copy and keep `v`, or reorder so this call is the last use of `v`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0209
